From 365808123b84b2325141fe55179b7df6916bf4ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:03:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild hero globe: dotted earth, flight arcs with airplanes,
 horizon-aware labels
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the cobe globe with a three.js scene in a new aqua/teal palette:

- Dotted landmass (~9.7k points from Natural Earth via world-atlas,
  scripts/generate-land-points.mjs) with the far hemisphere discarded in
  the shader; dark ocean sphere with a fresnel rim and a teal atmosphere.
- Ten flight routes draw themselves as great-circle arcs with an airplane
  riding the head of each arc (banked to the heading, grows on take-off,
  shrinks on landing), then the trail retracts. Pins pulse.
- Labels are positioned from the projected point every frame and fade/blur
  out the moment their city turns past the visible face — no more labels
  lingering for places behind the globe. No CSS anchor positioning, so it
  works in Safari/Firefox too.
- Drag to spin/tilt with inertia; renders only while on screen; honours
  prefers-reduced-motion (no spin, static full arcs, no planes).
- Removes the cobe dependency.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
